      "stdout": "Set the interpolation curve of an existing keyframe point.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --ref TEXT          Unified draft reference\r\n          --seg-id <SEG_ID[,SEG_ID...]> ... \r\n                              Target segment id; repeat --seg-id or pass a comma-separated list\r\n          --seg-type <TYPE[,TYPE...]> \r\n                              Target segment type(s): video, audio, text, sticker\r\n          --target-track <INDEX[,INDEX...]> \r\n                              Target track index(es)\r\n          --seg-index <INDEX[,INDEX...]> \r\n                              Comma-separated segment indexes within one target track, e.g.\r\n                              0,2,-1\r\n          --time-window <START,END> \r\n                              Select segments overlapping the half-open timeline window\r\n                              [start,end); start must be less than end\r\n          --animated-property TEXT \r\n                              Animated property: position-x, position-y, scale, scale-x,\r\n                              scale-y, rotation, opacity, or volume\r\n          --keyframe-type TEXT \r\n                              Advanced escape hatch: exact KFType* constant\r\n          --at <duration> REQUIRED \r\n                              Existing keyframe timestamp, e.g. 1s. Explicit unit required: us,\r\n                              ms, s, or min; bare numbers and m are invalid.\r\n          --curve TEXT        Curve alias:\r\n                              linear/ease-in/ease-out/ease-in-out/free-in/free-out/free-in-out\r\n          --curve-type TEXT   Advanced raw draft curveType enum. Unitless whole-number index.\r\n          --material-id TEXT  Material id 